cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "MB-CFD: MRI-driven moving-boundary CFD for patient-specific aortic hemodynamics (svMultiPhysics)"
authors:
  - family-names: Halter
    given-names: Elie
    email: elie.halter@gmail.com
  - family-names: Colombo
    given-names: Monika
    affiliation: "Aarhus University, Department of Mechanical and Production Engineering"
abstract: >-
  Open-source pipeline for moving-boundary versus rigid-wall CFD of the patient-specific
  thoracic aorta from 4D-flow MRI, run with the official, unmodified svMultiPhysics.
  One segmented phase is propagated to every cardiac phase by image registration (Elastix);
  the wall motion is imposed on the wall, faded to zero over 12 mm next to the fixed caps,
  and the interior mesh is moved by the solver's mesh equation (FSI equation with a fluid
  domain only). Gmsh meshing, conversion to the official solver input, analytic benchmarks,
  and tools for re-timing the wall motion, building rigid references at any cardiac phase
  and computing volume-weighted lumen means are included.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - moving boundary
  - arbitrary Lagrangian-Eulerian
  - aortic hemodynamics
  - 4D-flow MRI
  - image registration
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Elie-Halter/mb_cfd_pipeline"
